{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Data Acquisition", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to describe data acquisition procedures", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.  Understand information about data and its structure in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.   Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Action Verbs Related to Data Acquisition.", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Action verbs are activities people, animals, or things perform. There are some action verbs we use when we talk about data acquisition. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When we press a key, we are sending a signal.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When we move the mouse, it sends a signal that permits us to see the cursor on the screen.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Digital cameras also convert light levels, when downloading a picture it becomes understandable and easy to interpret as digital images.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We use many action verbs when we talk about data acquisition, because data acquisition implies the performance of certain actions in order to obtain data.<br/><br/>  Examples: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">The DAQ devices <span class=\"strong\">turn</span> data <span class=\"strong\">into</span>  digital representations. <dr/> A computer is able to <span class=\"strong\">manipulate</span> the digital representations.</span><br/><br/>  The chart below shows some examples of action verbs related to computer science.<br/>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Action Verbs Related to Data Acquisition</div>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Turn into\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Devices <span class=\\\"strong\\\">turn</span> measures <span class=\\\"strong\\\">into</span> digital forms.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Move\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When we <span class=\\\"strong\\\">move</span> the mouse the cursor receives the information and obeys.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Design \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Developers <span class=\\\"strong\\\">design</span> instruments to collect real-time data.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Convert \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Digital cameras <span class=\\\"strong\\\">convert</span> the light they detect into digital images.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Send  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The computer devices <span class=\\\"strong\\\">send</span> signals that are stored in a memory buffer.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Press\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When you <span class=\\\"strong\\\">press</span> a key, you send a signal to the computer.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Articles a/an vs. the, with Countable and Uncountable Nouns.", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are two types of articles in English, definite and indefinite; those articles accompany countable nouns and uncountable nouns.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Data acquisition is the process of collecting real-time data.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Data acquisition consist of recording facts from reality using a device, (a microphone, or a recorder).", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It sends a signal that allows us to see the cursor on the screen.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The computer processes the data and presents it on the computer screen.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Indefinite articles are the articles <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\"> \u201ca\u201d </span> or <span class=\"strong\">\u201can\u201d</span></span>. The difference between them is that you use <span class=\"strong\">\u201ca\u201d</span> with nouns starting with a consonant sound, and you use <span class=\"strong\">\u201can\u201d</span> with nouns starting with a vowel sound.<br/><br/> Examples:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">A</span> program. <br/> <span class=\"strong\">An</span> operation. </span><br/><br/> The article <span class=\"strong\">a/an</span> means one. For that reason, we only use them with countable singular nouns. <br/> Remember uncountable nouns cannot be counted, so do not use <span class=\"strong\">a/an</span> with uncountable nous.<br/><br/>  When you want to talk about nonspecific uncountable nouns, you don't use any article.<br/><br/>  Examples:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Inheritance</span> is one of the advantages of abstract data types.<br/><br/>   You can also use the definite article <span class=\"strong\">\u201cthe\u201d </span> when the speaker and the listener know exactly what we're talking about.<br/><br/>  Examples:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">The</span>  new program. <br/><span class=\"strong\"> The</span> freelance developers. <br/><br/></span> We can use the article <span class=\"strong\"> \u201cthe\u201d </span> with singular nouns, plural, and uncountable, when we talk about something explicitly and concrete. <br/><br/> Examples: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I bought <span class=\"strong\">the</span> last version of that software. <br/> We need <span class=\"strong\">the</span> new software urgently. <br/> I have to abstract <span class=\"strong\">the</span> datum. </span><br/>   ", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Common Collocations in Computer Science.", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Collocations are groups of words or statements that usually come together. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When we move the mouse, it sends a signal that allows us to see the cursor on the screen when navigating websites.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "In the computer science jargon there are several collocations. Let's have a look at some of the most common:<br/>  <strong>Hard copy:</strong> a printed copy of a document.<br/> <strong>Download a picture:</strong> to save a picture in your computer. You can also download files, music, movies, etc.<br/> <strong>Send an attachment:</strong> to deliver a document usually via e-mail. <br/> <strong>Receive spam:</strong> to get an unpleasant mail usually an advertisement, or a virus. <br/> <strong>Navigate websites:</strong> to visit sites on the internet.<br/>  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Digital cameras also convert light levels, when downloading a picture it becomes understandable and easy to interpret as digital images.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " It is represented by using different types of software stored in the memory or in any other hard-copy output device.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "screen ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the part of the computer where you can see the information displayed ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It sends a signal that allows us to see the cursor on the screen.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "environment ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "factors, in this case, surrounding data ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In certain environments (especially in the field of science and engineering), data acquisition devices help people collect real-time representations.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "display ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to show ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The datum is usually sent to a computer which uses software to process and display the data using graphs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "device ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an electronic mechanism  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Data acquisition consists of recording facts from reality using a device.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n3le01ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " resource ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "supply, asset", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The datum is usually sent to a computer which uses software to process and display the data using graphs, or oth